+Iterative Octree Traversal is a CPU-based ray traversal algorithm for Sparse Voxel Octrees (SVO) that uses a fixed-size stack to manage traversal state, handling valid internal nodes, leaf nodes, and empty space by casting rays to the next occupied voxel [S2, unofficial]. It employs a two-phase approach: a register-based DDA with bit-masked coordinate tracking for upper octree levels, and a slab-boundary-based stack traversal for deeper nodes [S1, unofficial][S2, unofficial].
 
